# libFuzzer dictionary for pty_login_scan_fuzzer (pty_screen's login-output
# scanners). Every interesting branch is gated on a literal token — the `https://`
# URL prefix, the OSC 8 escape framing, the authorize path markers, the known auth
# host suffixes and the token key. Atheris' random FuzzedDataProvider bytes never
# synthesise these, so without the dict (and the seed corpus) the harness sits at
# ~11 edges, fuzzing only the no-match path. See fuzz/README.md.
"https://"
"http://"
# authorize-endpoint path markers (matched against the PATH only)
"oauth/authorize"
"/cai/oauth/authorize"
"/authorize"
"?redirect_uri="
# known auth host suffixes, and the docs/marketing prefixes that must NOT win
"claude.ai"
"claude.com"
"anthropic.com"
"console.anthropic.com"
"platform.claude.com"
"docs."
"help."
"support."
"www."
# trailing characters `_clean_url` trims back off a matched URL
"."
")"
"\""
# The urlsplit ValueError `_url_host`/`_url_path` guard is the INVALID-IPv6-BRACKET one,
# not the `.port` case (neither helper reads `.port`, so a bad port never raises there).
# An unterminated `[` is what reaches the guard.
"https://[::1/"
"https://[bad/"
"[::1]"
":99999999999999/"
# OSC 8 hyperlink framing: ESC ] 8 ; <params> ; <URI> (ST | BEL)
"\x1b]8;;"
"\x1b]8;id=1;"
"\x1b\x5c"
"\x07"
# generic CSI/SGR noise the ANSI strip must remove first
"\x1b["
"\x1b[0m"
# the printed long-lived credential
"CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN="
